# See https://docs.github.com/articles/about-codeowners for syntax.
# Order matters — later matches take precedence, so the most specific rules
# are listed after the package-wide rules.
#
# NOTE: mirrors the same note in thyn-ai/algenta-sdk's CODEOWNERS. The
# thyn-ai org has exactly one member today (@angelatgithub) and no teams.
# Every entry below is that one real account, not a placeholder — replace
# with real teams (@thyn-ai/python-integrations-maintainers,
# @thyn-ai/ts-integrations-maintainers, @thyn-ai/contract-owners) as soon as
# a second maintainer joins. Until then, do NOT turn on branch protection's
# "Require review from Code Owners" — GitHub blocks a PR author from
# approving their own PR, so a solo-owner CODEOWNERS with that setting on
# would make every PR unmergeable by the only person who can open one.

/python/       @angelatgithub
/typescript/   @angelatgithub

# The no-engine-dependency check and the shared tool-profile contract are the
# two things this entire repository exists to keep true. A PR touching
# either gets flagged for deliberate review rather than being mergeable as
# an incidental part of a routine integration-package PR.
/scripts/check-no-engine-dependency.py   @angelatgithub
/contracts/                               @angelatgithub

# Workflow files (including the SDK-release sync receiver) are as
# security-sensitive as the code they run.
/.github/ @angelatgithub
